    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Language focus",
     "title": "will for roles and promises",
     "steps": [
      [
       "give a role",
       "You <b>will be</b> the lookout. Rolando, you <b>will throw</b> the lifebuoy."
      ],
      [
       "accept it",
       "<b>I'll</b> keep pointing. <b>I'll</b> throw it."
      ],
      [
       "shout",
       "Man overboard, <b>starboard side</b>! (no verb)"
      ]
     ],
     "paras": [
      "In an emergency the person in charge gives roles with <b>You will…</b>. You answer with <b>I'll…</b> + the action: short, so everyone knows it's done.",
      "The first shout has no verb: what + where. <b>Man overboard, port side!</b>"
     ],
     "avoid": "You are going to be lookout? (sounds like a question) · OK OK (without saying what you'll do)"
    },
